            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "The change is small, well\u2011scoped, and follows the established \"toggle + Vuex action\" pattern in the file. I noted a few consistency, a11y, and design issues worth addressing before merge."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "@a.nikhil@ibm.com\nBasic Auth section appears correctly when HTTPBasicAuth property is present in AccountService\nDisable \u2192 curl returns 401 (Basic Auth blocked) \u2705\nRe-enable \u2192 curl returns 200 (Basic Auth restored) \u2705\nWebUI session remains active after disable (expected \u2014 session token based) \u2705"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/locales/en-US.json",
                    "line": 809,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "missing updates to other language files."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/locales/en-US.json",
                    "line": 809,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/locales/en-US.json",
                    "line": 810,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "This should describe the feature, not the action.  Consider `\"HTTP Basic authentication\"`"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/locales/en-US.json",
                    "line": 810,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/locales/en-US.json",
                    "line": 811,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "try to describe feature in the affirmative, or enabled state:  \"Allow authentication to the Redfish/HTTPS interface using HTTP Basic Auth.\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/locales/en-US.json",
                    "line": 811,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/SecurityAndAccess/PoliciesStore.js",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "rename to `basicAuthEnabled` for consistency with other getters above.\nBonus points to rename to `HTTPBasicAuth` for a Redfish-first approach to reference the `AccountService` schema.\n\nAlso distilling to a boolean is not really handling the Enum: `\"Enabled\" | \"Disabled\" | \"Unadvertised\"`"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/SecurityAndAccess/PoliciesStore.js",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Agree with the first point and the changes are made.\nBut for 2nd point, What will the toggle state if the redfish returns `\"Unadvertised\"`?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/SecurityAndAccess/PoliciesStore.js",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "It is enabled.\n\nBut in that case it would be nice to let the user know that the service does not include `Basic` in the value of the `WWW-Authenticate` HTTP response header.\nThe lack of advertisement prevents some clients from accessing the service with HTTP Basic authentication, such as web browsers."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/SecurityAndAccess/PoliciesStore.js",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Will raise a follow-up PR for handling Unadvertised."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/SecurityAndAccess/PoliciesStore.js",
                    "line": 63,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "This catch swallows real failures (like 500) and falsely reports \"not supported.\" Consider distinguishing 404 / missing-property from generic error."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/store/modules/SecurityAndAccess/PoliciesStore.js",
                    "line": 63,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/SecurityAndAccess/Policies/Policies.vue",
                    "line": 140,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "perhaps better placed with other toggles, like after SSH or IPMI?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/SecurityAndAccess/Policies/Policies.vue",
                    "line": 140,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Agree!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/SecurityAndAccess/Policies/Policies.vue",
                    "line": 147,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "For consistency, use `visually-hidden-focusable` to allow keyboard access."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/SecurityAndAccess/Policies/Policies.vue",
                    "line": 147,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/SecurityAndAccess/Policies/Policies.vue",
                    "line": 266,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "This matches the pattern used in this file, but this is awkward.\n`v-model` requires 2-way binding, hence this pattern.\nInstead use `:model-value` which lets the computed be a read-only getter.\n\nIf you update this, a good follow-up is to fix the other 4 instances in this file."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/SecurityAndAccess/Policies/Policies.vue",
                    "line": 266,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Started with basic Auth, Follow-up MR will be raised for policies."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/SecurityAndAccess/Policies/Policies.vue",
                    "line": 276,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "Cleaner alternative would be to add a `basicAuthSupported` state field + getter, set it from `getBasicAuth`, and use `v-if=\"basicAuthSupported\"` in the template. Keeps presence/value concerns separate and avoids per\u2011instance state."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/views/SecurityAndAccess/Policies/Policies.vue",
                    "line": 276,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
